      "text": "We can use the distance formula to find the distance between two points in the coordinate plane. The formula is:\n\ndistance = √((x2 - x1)² + (y2 - y1)²)\n\nIn this case, point 1 is (-3, -4) and point 2 is (4, -5). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\ndistance = √((4 - (-3))² + (-5 - (-4))²)\n         = √(7² + 1²)\n         = √(49 + 1)\n         = √50\n         = 5√2\n\nSo, the distance between the points (-3, -4) and (4, -5) is 5√2 units.",
