      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the distance between two points in a coordinate plane, we can use the distance formula:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$\n\nSubstituting $(x_1, y_1) = (-3, -4)$ and $(x_2, y_2) = (4, -5)$ into the formula, we get:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{(4 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - (-4))^2}$\n\nSimplifying inside the parentheses:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{(7)^2 + (-1)^2}$\n\nContinuing to simplify:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{49 + 1}$\n\nAdding the numbers inside the square root:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{50}$\n\nTo simplify $\\sqrt{50}$, we can factor out a perfect square:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{5 \\times 10}$\n\nFurther simplifying, we have:\n\n$\\text{distance} = \\sqrt{5} \\times \\sqrt{10}$\n\nSince $\\sqrt{10}$ cannot be simplified anymore, the final answer is:\n\n$\\boxed{\\sqrt{50}}$",
